# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# The project window: a program is what a person works on, and the
# files it is made of are LISTED rather than remembered.  Opening a row
# opens an editor window of its own; opening it again brings that
# window back rather than making a second one onto the same document;
# and the Window menu is the one place that says which of them has work
# in it that nothing has saved.
#
# The project is a FOLDER with a project.tiku in it, and the shell's
# own panel is how it is opened -- the IDE never learns to walk a
# filesystem.
wait 25
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Applications
wait 4
expect-menu TikuIDE
menu-pick TikuIDE
wait 150
expect-title Project
note the application says what it is when asked: the About box stands
note until it has been read, and Escape puts it away
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu About TikuIDE
menu-pick About TikuIDE
wait 30
expect-title About TikuIDE
note asked for again it comes FORWARD rather than doubling
click-window Project
wait 8
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick About TikuIDE
wait 30
expect-title About TikuIDE
expect-windows 3
key Escape
wait 20
expect-no-title About
note the project is handed over by the shell's panel, as every file an
note application is given comes to it
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu Open Project…
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
expect-title TikuTracker: Open
click 400 248
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
expect-no-title TikuTracker: Open
note the list travels over the group's NAME: Down from nothing lands on
note the first FILE, because a heading is not something to open
click-window Project
wait 8
key Down
wait 8
key Return
wait 90
expect-title blink.bas
note a second file opens a window of its own -- by MOUSE this time:
note two clicks on its row are the same door Return is
click-window Project
wait 8
click 400 203
wait 6
click 400 203
wait 90
expect-title util.bas
note and the Window menu names them both
click-window Project
wait 8
click 132 8
wait 8
expect-menu blink.bas|util.bas|
menu-pick blink.bas
wait 30
expect-title blink.bas
note typing marks the document, and the mark shows in the one list
note that says where a person's unsaved work is
key h shift
key i
wait 20
click-window Project
wait 8
click 132 8
wait 8
expect-menu blink.bas (changed)
menu-pick blink.bas (changed)
wait 30
expect-title blink.bas
note asking for a file already open brings ITS window back rather than
note opening the same document twice
click-window Project
wait 8
key Up
wait 6
key Return
wait 40
expect-title blink.bas
expect-windows 4
note saving puts the words in the file and takes the mark off again
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Save blink.bas
wait 30
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/blink.bas Hi
click-window Project
wait 8
click 132 8
wait 8
expect-menu blink.bas|util.bas|
note taking a row of the Window menu is how the OTHER window is
note reached, and it puts the menu away with the same gesture
menu-pick util.bas
wait 30
expect-title util.bas
note closing the project asks ONCE, and names what is at stake: the
note question is the application's own, over its own window, and it
note stands until somebody answers it
key q
wait 20
click-window Project
wait 8
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Close Project
wait 30
expect-title Project
note Escape presses Cancel, the safe road: everything is still standing
key Escape
wait 20
expect-title Project
note every window it opened is still there, and still reachable by the
note list that names them
expect-windows 4
click 132 8
wait 8
menu-pick blink.bas
wait 30
expect-title blink.bas
note asked again, Return presses the default and the project goes,
note taking every window it opened with it
click-window Project
wait 8
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Close Project
wait 30
key Return
wait 40
expect-no-title blink.bas
expect-no-title util.bas
expect-no-title Project
